<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- NuGet packaging metadata -->
    <Description>Foundational primitives for the SharedKernel: Result&lt;T&gt;, Error, ErrorCodes, IClock, SmartEnum, ValidationResult. Carries one first-party Microsoft.Extensions dependency (Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions), used solely by the optional ClockExtensions.AddClock() DI convenience extension. AOT-compatible.</Description>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>This package ships as part of the platform's single, repo-wide MinVer-derived version (see root CLAUDE.md's "Package Versioning" section) — the notes below describe what changed and why, not a package-specific version number.

Notable change (WO-059 / P-384): added ErrorType.Forbidden and the corresponding Error.Forbidden(string code, string message) factory, mirroring BusinessRule's addition pattern (P-042). Forbidden represents a caller who is generally permitted to attempt an operation, but for whom this specific instance/condition is not satisfied — maps to HTTP 403 Forbidden at the presentation layer. Distinct from Unauthorized (not permitted to attempt this at all — HTTP 401) and from BusinessRule (a domain invariant violation, not an authorization/permission gate). Purely additive: no existing ErrorType member's numeric value changed and no existing Error factory's signature changed. COMPILE-TIME RISK: a downstream consumer with an exhaustive switch/switch expression over ErrorType carrying no discard/default arm will fail to compile after picking up this change, because a new enum member now exists — this is a compile-time signal, not a runtime break; add a discard/default arm or an explicit Forbidden case to restore exhaustiveness. No new ErrorCodes constant was added for it — unlike BusinessRule's companion ErrorCodes.Domain.RuleViolated, no consuming phase requested a shared code constant for Forbidden.

See 01.Core/CLAUDE.md's changelog for the full history of every change to this package.</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <PackageTags>shared-kernel;result;railway-oriented;clock;smart-enum;aot</PackageTags>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
